      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "William Murphy from Dublin, Ireland",
      "description": "Fota Wildlife Park is set on 70 acres on the scenic Fota Island in the heart of Cork Harbour only 15 minutes from Cork City by train.\nIn 2005 I visited Fota Park in Cork but the weather was so bad that I ended up with no usable photographs. This visit the conditions were almost as bad with few breaks in the rain. Howevr this time using Lightroom 4 has made it possible to process most of the photographs but the images are inclined to be a bit soft.\nThe park is not like an ordinary zoo because you can come face to face with free roaming animals and birds from all parts of the world. So whether it's a kangaroo that hops in front of you or a ring tailed lemur which jumps down from a tree, each visit is sure to bring its own fantastic memories.\n\nI hope that you enjoy this series of photographs",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 6 June 2012, 14:30",
